WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
In this lesson, we sort every dollar into two lists.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Cash coming in is money that actually lands in your account.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Record customer payments on the day you expect them to arrive, not the day you send the invoice.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Include deposits and retainers.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Include loans or grants only when the money is received.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
And include any HST refunds.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Cash going out is every payment that leaves your account.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Rent, payroll and insurance.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Supplier bills and inventory.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
HST remittances and tax instalments.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Loan payments, and what you pay yourself.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Now put it together.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Start with your opening cash: five thousand dollars.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Add cash coming in: twelve thousand.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Subtract cash going out: fourteen thousand five hundred.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Your closing cash is two thousand five hundred dollars.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Your turn. In the next lesson, download the worksheet.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Then fill in one month, week by week.
